  "question": {
    "text": "In a series <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>L</mi><mi>R</mi></math> circuit with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>R</mi></math>,&nbsp;power factor is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>. If a capacitor of capacitance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi></math> with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>L</mi></msub></math> is added to the circuit the power factor becomes <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>. The ratio of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> will be :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
